{"story":{"what":"The change hardens TypeCollector.GetObjectInfo so that invalid key layouts no longer throw. A member whose key kind does not match the others is now skipped after the mixed-key diagnostic is reported. Duplicate int or string keys are no longer added to the member dictionaries a second time. The default constructor search now orders candidates by ascending parameter count instead of descending. The change also adds analyzer tests and execution tests for SuppressSourceGeneration = true types, plus a README section on which diagnostics still apply to such types.","why":"Requirement MP-2234 says the analyzer stopped reporting diagnostics for [MessagePackObject(SuppressSourceGeneration = true)] types after 3.1.1. In the code, a duplicate or mixed key reached Dictionary.Add with a key that was already present, which throws. That exception would abort analysis instead of producing MsgPack005. The fix reports the problem and keeps analysis going, and the tests check that suppressed types get their diagnostics again.","touches":[{"symbol":"TypeCollector.GetObjectInfo","file":"src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs","note":"Skips members with a mismatched key kind, guards the dictionary adds against duplicate keys, and changes the constructor ordering to ascending parameter count."},{"symbol":"SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests","file":"tests/MessagePack.SourceGenerator.Tests/SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.cs","note":"New analyzer tests for diagnostics on suppressed types and on a non-suppressed duplicate-key type."},{"symbol":"SuppressedSourceGenerationTests","file":"tests/MessagePack.SourceGenerator.ExecutionTests/SuppressedSourceGenerationTests.cs","note":"New execution tests: no generated formatter for a suppressed type, and a round trip through the dynamic resolver."},{"symbol":"Opting out of source generation","file":"README.md","note":"New README section on which analyzer checks apply to suppressed types and which do not."}]},"claims":[{"requirementItemId":"N1","text":"In both the property loop and the field loop of the key-attribute path, after DoNotMixStringAndIntKeys is reported for a member whose key kind differs from the first member's, the loop continues. The member is not added to intMembers or stringMembers, and it is not recursively collected.","kind":"behaviour","hunkIds":["h2","h5"],"pathGlob":null,"citations":[{"file":"src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs","side":"new","startLine":1005,"endLine":1009,"quote":"continue; // The key kind does not match the other members; the diagnostic is reported, so skip this member."},{"file":"src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs","side":"new","startLine":1145,"endLine":1149,"quote":"continue; // The key kind does not match the other members; the diagnostic is reported, so skip this member."}]},{"requirementItemId":"N1","text":"For both properties and fields, intMembers.Add and stringMembers.Add now run only when the key is not already present. A duplicate key is still reported as KeysMustBeUnique, but it no longer throws a duplicate-key exception from Dictionary.Add. The first member with a given key is the one kept.","kind":"behaviour","hunkIds":["h3","h4","h6","h7"],"pathGlob":null,"citations":[{"file":"src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs","side":"new","startLine":1023,"endLine":1026,"quote":"if (!intMembers.ContainsKey(member.IntKey))
