ts check that GeneratedMessagePackResolver returns no formatter for a suppressed type. They also check that the type round-trips through MessagePackSerializerOptions.Standard.","kind":"test","hunkIds":["h9"],"pathGlob":null,"citations":[{"file":"tests/MessagePack.SourceGenerator.ExecutionTests/SuppressedSourceGenerationTests.cs","side":"new","startLine":20,"endLine":24,"quote":"Assert.Null(GeneratedMessagePackResolver.Instance.GetFormatter<SuppressedSourceGenerationType>());"},{"file":"tests/MessagePack.SourceGenerator.ExecutionTests/SuppressedSourceGenerationTests.cs","side":"new","startLine":29,"endLine":35,"quote":"byte[] bytes = MessagePackSerializer.Serialize(value, MessagePackSerializerOptions.Standard);"}]},{"requirementItemId":"F1","text":"The README gains an Opting out of source generation section. It lists MsgPack004, 005, 015, 003 and 012 as still reported for suppressed types, and MsgPack011, 016 and 017 as not reported.","kind":"docs","hunkIds":["h1"],"pathGlob":null,"citations":[{"file":"README.md","side":"new","startLine":1620,"endLine":1626,"quote":"The analyzer still validates these types, because they are serialized at run time and must still have a valid contract:"},{"file":"README.md","side":"new","startLine":1627,"endLine":1633,"quote":"The analyzer does not report the partial-class requirement ([MsgPack011](doc/analyzers/MsgPack011.md)) or the AOT-only checks ([MsgPack016](doc/analyzers/MsgPack016.md) and [MsgPack017](doc/analyzers/MsgPack017.md)) for these types, because they only apply when a formatter is generated."}]}]}
